> · <!-- -->2015-02-26<!-- --> ·<!-- --> <!-- -->3<!-- --> min ·<!-- --> <a class="transition-colors hover:text-primary" href="../pro-tips">pro-tips</a></p><h1 class="mt-3 max-w-[24ch] text-[clamp(1.9rem,3.5vw+0.8rem,3rem)] leading-[1.15] font-normal tracking-tight">Awesome Looking Terminal With Oh-My-Zsh</h1><p class="mt-6 max-w-[52ch] text-xl font-light text-muted-foreground">My terminal setup on Ubuntu in 2015: Guake, Zsh with Oh-My-Zsh, the agnoster theme with a patched font, and plugins such as artisan completion.</p><div class="mt-10 max-w-md" aria-label="Entries over the past year"><svg class="block h-auto w-full overflow-visible" viewBox="0 0 480 40" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0.0,34.0 L9.2,34.0 L18.5,34.0 L27.7,34.0 L36.9,34.0 L46.2,34.0 L55.4,34.0 L64.6,34.0 L73.8,34.0 L83.1,34.0 L92.3,34.0 L101.5,34.0 L110.8,34.0 L120.0,34.0 L129.2,34.0 L138.5,34.0 L147.7,34.0 L156.9,34.0 L166.2,34.0 L175.4,34.0 L184.6,34.0 L193.8,34.0 L203.1,34.0 L212.3,34.0 L221.5,34.0 L230.8,34.0 L240.0,34.0 L249.2,34.0 L258.5,34.0 L267.7,34.0 L276.9,34.0 L286.2,34.0 L295.4,34.0 L304.6,34.0 L313.8,34.0 L323.1,34.0 L332.3,34.0 L341.5,34.0 L350.8,34.0 L360.0,34.0 L369.2,6.0 L378.5,34.0 L387.7,34.0 L396.9,27.8 L406.2,34.0 L415.4,34.0 L424.6,34.0 L433.8,30.9 L443.1,30.9 L452.3,24.7 L461.5,34.0 L470.8,34.0 L480.0,34.0" class="fill-none stroke-border" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg><p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider text-muted-foreground uppercase">written before the past year<!-- --> · entry <!-- -->14<!-- --> <!-- -->of <!-- -->37<!-- --> · <!-- -->16<!-- --> in <!-- -->the past year</p></div><ul class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><li><a class="transition-colors hover:text-primary" href="../zsh">#<!-- -->zsh</a></li><li><a class="transition-colors hover:text-primary" href="../terminal">#<!-- -->terminal</a></li><li><a class="transition-colors hover:text-primary" href="../linux">#<!-- -->linux</a></li><li><a class="transition-colors hover:text-primary" href="../productivity">#<!-- -->productivity</a></li></ul></header><div data-slot="alert" role="note" class="group/alert relative grid w-full gap-0.5 rounded-lg border text-left text-sm has-data-[slot=alert-action]:relative has-data-[slot=alert-action]:pr-18 has-[&gt;svg]:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] has-[&gt;svg]:gap-x-2 *:[svg]:row-span-2 *:[svg]:translate-y-0.5 *:[svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 text-card-foreground mb-10 max-w-3xl border-tint-ochre/30 bg-tint-ochre/10 px-4 py-3 *:[svg]:text-tint-ochre"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-rotate-ccw-clock lucide-history" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 9-9 9.75 9.75 0 0 0-6.74 2.74L3 8"/><path d="M3 3v5h5"/><path d="M12 7v5l4 2"/></svg><div data-slot="alert-title" class="font-medium group-has-[&gt;svg]/alert:col-start-2 [&amp;_a]:underline [&amp;_a]:underline-offset-3 [&amp;_a]:hover:text-foreground">This article is out of date</div><div data-slot="alert-description" class="text-sm text-balance md:text-pretty [&amp;_a]:underline [&amp;_a]:underline-offset-3 [&amp;_a]:hover:text-foreground [&amp;_p:not(:last-child)]:mb-4 text-foreground">Written in 2015. Versions, APIs and advice may have changed since.</div></div><article class="prose-ui w-full max-w-3xl pb-10"><p>A lot of people asked me after reading my article <a title="A Brief Introduction to Laravel Envoy" href="../07/brief-introduction-laravel-envoy">A Brief Introduction to Laravel Envoy</a>, how do I get my terminal window to look so awesome. It’s not that hard as it may look like, I keep it simple. Here is what I use:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://github.com/Guake/guake" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Guak Terminal">Guake terminal</a></li>
<li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Z_shell" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Z Shell">ZSH (Z shell)</a></li>
<li><a href="http://ohmyz.sh/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Oh-My-Zsh">Oh-My-Zsh</a></li>
</ul>
<p>and of course Ubuntu GNU/Linux.</p>
<p>As a developer, you can increase your productivity by using terminal. But, sometimes people are just too lazy to type long commands over and over again. And it gets even more boring if you repeat same stuff every single day, at the job, at home, everywhere. That’s the primary reason why so many people are so scared of the terminal. But, it does not have to be that way. Few years ago I was so excited when I “discovered” <em><strong>Oh-My-Zsh</strong></em>. And almost instantly I switched <em>Bash</em> with <em>ZSH</em>.</p>
<p>Here are the main reasons why I chose <em>ZSH</em> instead of <em>Bash</em> :</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>incredibly powerful, context based tab completion handling</strong></li>
<li><strong>pattern matching on steroids</strong></li>
<li><strong>really great community-driven frameworks available</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>There are two major frameworks available for <em>ZSH</em> , <a href="https://github.com/sorin-ionescu/prezto" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Prezto - Instantly Awesome Zsh">Prezto</a> and <a href="https://github.com/robbyrussell/oh-my-zsh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Oh-My-Zsh Github">Oh-My-Zsh</a>. Personally, I prefer <em><strong>Oh-My-Zsh</strong></em> , but Pretzo have it’s own advantages to.</p>
<p>Oh-My-Zsh is an open source, community-driven framework for managing your ZSH configuration. It comes bundled with a ton of helpful functions, helpers, plugins, themes, and a few things that make you shout…</p>
<h2 id="installing-zsh-and-oh-my-zsh">Installing ZSH and Oh-My-Zsh</h2>
<p>Installation of <em>ZSH</em> is pretty simple, on Debian/Ubuntu just enter:</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><div class="mb-3 flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-dashed pr-3 pb-3 pl-3 font-mono text-xs"><span class="min-w-0 truncate text-syntax-text">terminal</span><span class="text-syntax-comment max-sm:hidden">1<!-- --> <!-- -->line</span><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary ml-auto">copy</button></div><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"><span class="hl-f">sudo</span><span class="hl-s"> apt-get</span><span class="hl-s"> install</span><span class="hl-s"> zsh</span></span></span></span></code></pre></div>
<p><em><strong>Oh-My-Zsh</strong></em> you can install with <em><strong>curl</strong></em> or <em><strong>wget,</strong></em> so make sure you have them installed:</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><div class="mb-3 flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-dashed pr-3 pb-3 pl-3 font-mono text-xs"><span class="min-w-0 truncate text-syntax-text">terminal</span><span class="text-syntax-comment max-sm:hidden">1<!-- --> <!-- -->line</span><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary ml-auto">copy</button></div><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"><span class="hl-f">curl</span><span class="hl-s"> -L</span><span class="hl-s"> https://raw.github.com/robbyrussell/oh-my-zsh/master/tools/install.sh</span><span class="hl-k"> |</span><span class="hl-f"> sh</span></span></span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>or with <em><strong>wget</strong></em> :</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><div class="mb-3 flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-dashed pr-3 pb-3 pl-3 font-mono text-xs"><span class="min-w-0 truncate text-syntax-text">terminal</span><span class="text-syntax-comment max-sm:hidden">1<!-- --> <!-- -->line</span><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary ml-auto">copy</button></div><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"><span class="hl-f">wget</span><span class="hl-s"> https://raw.github.com/robbyrussell/oh-my-zsh/master/tools/install.sh</span><span class="hl-s"> -O</span><span class="hl-s"> -</span><span class="hl-k"> |</span><span class="hl-f"> sh</span></span></span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>For more detailed installation instruction visit the official page.</p>
<h2 id="themify-your-promt">Themify Your Promt</h2>
<p>Another great thing with <em><strong>Oh-My-Zsh</strong></em> is that you have a ton of useful <a href="https://github.com/robbyrussell/oh-my-zsh/wiki/Themes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Oh-My-Zsh Themes">themes</a> and <a href="https://github.com/robbyrussell/oh-my-zsh/wiki/Plugins" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Oh-My-Zsh Plugins">plugins</a> you can use to customize your prompt. I use <a href="https://github.com/robbyrussell/oh-my-zsh/wiki/Themes#agnoster" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Agnoster Theme">agnoster</a> as my default theme. To setup this theme, just download and install one of the patched fonts for Vim-Powerline. For me <a href="https://github.com/powerline/fonts/tree/master/DejaVuSansMono" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>DejaVuSansMono</em></a> is good enough. After you have installed patched font, edit ~/.zshrc and set <em><strong>agnoster</strong></em> for theme:</p>
<div data-code-frame="true" class="not-prose relative my-8 bg-[var(--p-code-block-color-bg)] py-4 text-sm leading-[1.7] text-syntax-text"><div class="mb-3 flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-dashed pr-3 pb-3 pl-3 font-mono text-xs"><span class="min-w-0 truncate text-syntax-text">~/.zshrc</span><span class="text-syntax-comment max-sm:hidden">bash · <!-- -->5<!-- --> <!-- -->lines</span><button type="button" class="font-mono text-xs text-syntax-comment transition-colors hover:text-primary ml-auto">copy</button></div><pre class="overflow-x-auto font-code"><code class="block w-max min-w-full"><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"><span class="hl-f">...</span></span></span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"></span></span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"><span class="hl-fg">ZSH_THEME</span><span class="hl-k">=</span><span class="hl-se">"agnoster"</span></span></span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"></span></span></span><span class="flex min-h-[1.7em] pr-4"><span class="whitespace-pre pl-3"><span class="line"><span class="hl-f">...</span></span></span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>Now, open <em><strong>Guake Preference</strong></em> and set default interpreter to /bin/zsh :</p>
<p><img src="https://media.bosnadev.com/hub/e112718c08d2ea80/2015-02-guake-properties.webp" alt="Guake General Properties" width="643" height="651" loading="lazy" decoding="async">and in the <em><strong>Appearance</strong></em> tab your patched font:</p>
